## Description

Implement `catalyst-core`'s run-state parsing (`core-CONTRACT-000003-UVqkd7cL`) and
`catalyst-host-vscode`'s live "Runs" tree section (`vscode-RUNMONITOR-
001`), completing the roadmap's last surface.

## Acceptance

- `catalyst-core` parses `runs/*.md` into a typed list (id, status,
  command, started, a checklist of glyph-parsed steps, a ledger),
  included in `watchCorpus`'s update alongside the model, validation
  report, and proposals.
- An unrecognized checklist-line prefix is skipped, not thrown on — the
  parser stays tolerant of agent-authored content it doesn't control,
  same posture as every other parser in this package.
- `hasDrift(run)` is `true` iff any step's status is `drift`.
- The chain inspector tree shows a "Runs (N)" section; its label
  carries a visible `⚠️` marker whenever any run has drift, updating
  live as the watcher picks up the agent's own file edits — the
  concrete form of "a drift event is visible in the UI before the run
  completes."
- Read-only: the extension never creates or edits a run file.

## Notes

Targets two rules, same split as `REQ-000004-UVqkd7cL`: `core-CONTRACT-000003-UVqkd7cL` (the
parsing is real, independent core infrastructure — any future host
wants the same `Run`/`hasDrift` shape) and `vscode-RUNMONITOR-000001-UVqkd7cL` (the
VS Code UI built on top of it). Unlike `REQ-000004-UVqkd7cL`/`REQ-000005-UVqkd7cL`, there
is no write-path rule here — a run is never authored by this deployment's
own UI.
